 "strategy": {
  "summary": "Fade sudden, outsized moves a few minutes after they peak, day session only. Christensen, Oomen & Ren\u00f2 (\"The drift burst hypothesis\") find that short bursts of extreme drift in futures (about one a week in ES at their settings) mostly reverse within minutes: about 71% reverse over the next 5 minutes, drops more than spikes, and bursts on heavy volume for the time of day reverse most. Their study used tick data to 2017, mid-quotes and no costs; this is a simplified 1-minute version on traded prices.",
  "formula": "T = k-minute log return \u00f7 (local volatility \u00d7 \u221ak); fade when |T| peaks above the threshold",
  "rules": [
   {
    "label": "Signal",
    "text": "Over the last k minutes (3, 5 or 10): the log return, divided by the volatility of the 5k one-minute returns just before it (scaled by \u221ak). Everything stays inside one day session."
   },
   {
    "label": "Enter",
    "text": "When |T| has been above the threshold (3.5, 4, 4.5 or 5) and stops rising, trade against the burst at the next bar's open. Optional filters: the burst window's volume must be at least 1.5\u00d7, 2\u00d7 or 3\u00d7 the normal volume for those minutes of the day (20-day average); buy drops only; skip bursts around 08:30 and 10:00 ET releases and on Wednesdays 14:00\u201315:00 ET. At most one trade per day."
   },
   {
    "label": "Exit",
    "text": "After 5, 15 or 30 minutes at that bar's close, or at the session's last close if sooner. No stop."
   },
   {
    "label": "v2 additions",
    "text": "Entry timing: fade as soon as |T| crosses the threshold, one bar after it peaks (v1), or after two falling bars. Optional profit target at 0.5\u00d7 or 1.0\u00d7 the burst move back from the entry, and optional stop 1.0\u00d7 the burst move beyond it (a bar touching both counts as the stop). Up to 1 or 3 trades a day."
   },
   {
    "label": "Size",
    "text": "One position at a time, never held overnight. As many whole ES contracts as the account covers at full contract value (no leverage), starting from $1,000,000."
   }
  ],
