  "method": "Per bar size and side setting (long_only = long only, both = the finalists' actual long share): random intraday trades on random sessions at random times, never overlapping and always closed by the session's last bar, covering the target share of the validation window's bars. Trade lengths are drawn from that group's own validation trades; each trade is long with the group's actual long share (1.0 for long-only, 0.0 for short-only), else short. Same fills, slippage, commission and whole-contract sizing as the strategy; scored with the same daily-Sharpe and time-in-market code.",
  "curves": [],
  "text": "For every whole-percent time in market in each group's 2023\u20132024 range, 100 random runs trade ES at random times of the day session on random days, so they test whether the burst trigger matters. Each group is one side setting. Like the strategy, the random trades are intraday only, never overlap, and are always closed by the session's last bar. Their lengths are drawn from that group's own finalist trades, so trade counts and costs match. Buy-drops-only groups trade long; fade-both groups go long with the same share of trades their finalists did. They pay the same costs and use the same sizing and Sharpe math as the strategy."
